.TH KNOTS 1 "2026-09-30" "knots 1.18.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
knots \- multi-language code complexity analyzer with AI cost metrics
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B knots
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] [\fIFILE\fR...]
.br
.B knots
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] \fB\-\-compile\-commands\fR <\fIFILE\fR>
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B knots
is a fast multi-language code complexity analyzer built on tree-sitter.
It measures traditional complexity metrics alongside two AI-specific cost scores \(em
.B AIRD
(AI Reasoning Difficulty) and
.B AICP
(AI Context Pressure) \(em to identify which functions are genuinely expensive to
modify with AI assistance.
.PP
.B knots
computes the following metrics for each function:
.TP
.B McCabe Cyclomatic Complexity
Counts decision points (if, while, for, do, switch, ternary, logical operators).
Published definitions govern counting. Pinned comparisons and departures
are recorded in validation/README.md and docs/metrics-reference.rst.
.TP
.B Cognitive Complexity
Measures difficulty to understand code, emphasizing nesting and structural
complexity.
Based on the SonarSource specification.
.TP
.B Nesting Depth
Maximum nesting level of control structures.
.TP
.B SLOC
Source lines of code (non-blank, non-comment).
.TP
.B ABC Complexity
Assignment, Branch, Condition magnitude: sqrt(A\(S2 + B\(S2 + C\(S2).
.TP
.B Return Count
Number of return statements in a function.
.TP
.B Test Scoring
Multi-dimensional test difficulty metric across signature, dependency,
observable, implementation, and documentation axes.
.TP
.B External Calls
Count of unique identifier-form call targets not defined in the same translation
unit. Measures external dependency breadth (out-of-file functions and
function-like macros).
.TP
.B AIRD \(em AI Reasoning Difficulty
Normalized 0\(en100 score predicting how much reasoning effort an AI model needs
to safely modify a function.
Each positive term is capped at its ceiling: cognitive/75 times 55,
sloc/200 times 15, nesting/8 times 15, max(test_score, 0)/20 times 15,
and state_coupling/12 times 10; subtract capped max(doc_score, 0)/10 times 15.
The sum is rounded and clamped to 0\(en100. In recursive mode, file-level
Ce multiplies that score by 1 + min(Ce/10, 1) times 0.2, then rounds and clamps.
The Cognitive input includes all live preprocessor arms as written, unlike
the reported worst-configuration Cognitive metric.
Ceilings and the suggested gate of 85 are predominantly C-calibrated;
the nine-function pilot did not validate predictive accuracy.
.TP
.B AICP \(em AI Context Pressure
Normalized 0\(en100 score predicting how much context an AI model must load before
it can act. Complements AIRD: a function can be cheap to load but hard to reason
about, or expensive to load but trivial once context is assembled.
Formula: min(external_calls/20, 1) times 60 + min(sloc/200, 1) times 40
minus min(max(doc_score, 0)/10, 1) times 15, rounded and clamped to 0\(en100.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-r ", " \-\-recursive
Recursively process all supported source files in directories.
Headers, including .h, .hpp, .hxx and .ads, are included by default.
Detailed report files require \fB\-\-report\fR in multi-file text mode.
.TP
.BI \-l " LANG" ", " \-\-language " LANG"
Restrict analysis to files of the given language.
Repeatable to allow multiple languages (e.g.\&
.BR "\-l cpp \-l c \-l rust" ).
.I LANG
is matched case-insensitively against language names (e.g.\&
.BR rust ,
.BR c++ ,
.BR fortran )
and against any recognized extension alias (e.g.\&
.BR rs ,
.BR cpp ,
.BR f90 ).
Run
.B knots \-\-supported\-languages
to see the full list.
Mostly useful with
.BR \-\-recursive .
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Show detailed per-function analysis.
.TP
.BR \-m ", " \-\-matrix
Show testability matrix categorization.
Functions are placed into four quadrants:
QUICK WINS (low complexity, easy to test),
INVEST IN TESTS (high complexity, easy to test),
ADD DOCS (low complexity, hard to test),
REFACTOR (high complexity, hard to test).
.TP
.BI \-\-compile\-commands " FILE"
Use a
.I compile_commands.json
file (from CMake, Bear, etc.) to get the list of files to analyze.
C/C++ only \(em compilation databases are not produced by Rust, Python, or JavaScript toolchains.
Mutually exclusive with the positional \fIFILE\fR argument.
.TP
.BI \-\-include " FILE"
Include filter rules from a JSON file (whitelist).
See
.BR FILTERS
below.
.TP
.BI \-\-exclude " FILE"
Exclude filter rules from a JSON file (blacklist).
See
.BR FILTERS
below.
.TP
.BI \-\-format " FORMAT"
Output format. One of:
.RS
.TP
.B text
Human-readable output (default).
.TP
.B sarif
SARIF 2.1.0 JSON for VS Code / GitHub Code Scanning.
.TP
.B json
JSON array of per-function metrics.
.TP
.B ndjson
Newline-delimited JSON \(em one record per line, composable via find/xargs.
.TP
.B csv
CSV with header row.
.RE
.TP
.B \-\-score\-components
With \fB\-\-format\fR json, ndjson or csv, add AIRD's and AICP's
per\-term contributions, their pre\-clamp raw sums, AIRD before the
file\-level multiplier, the multiplier itself, and state_coupling
(extra JSON keys; trailing CSV columns). The default fields are unchanged. Ignored for text and sarif.
.TP
.BI \-\-mccabe\-threshold " N"
Exit 1 if any function exceeds this McCabe complexity.
.TP
.BI \-\-cognitive\-threshold " N"
Exit 1 if any function exceeds this cognitive complexity.
.TP
.BI \-\-nesting\-threshold " N"
Exit 1 if any function exceeds this nesting depth.
.TP
.BI \-\-sloc\-threshold " N"
Exit 1 if any function exceeds this SLOC count.
.TP
.BI \-\-abc\-threshold " F"
Exit 1 if any function exceeds this ABC magnitude.
.TP
.BI \-\-return\-threshold " N"
Exit 1 if any function exceeds this return count.
.TP
.BI \-\-aird\-threshold " N"
Exit 1 if any function exceeds this AIRD score.
Suggested value: 85, calibrated predominantly on C. See the metrics reference
and ADR-0003 before choosing project gates.
.TP
.BI \-\-aicp\-threshold " N"
Exit 1 if any function exceeds this AICP score.
.TP
.BI \-\-external\-calls\-threshold " N"
Exit 1 if any function exceeds this external call count.
.TP
.BI \-j " N" ", " \-\-jobs " N"
Number of parallel analysis threads when processing multiple files.
.B 0
(the default) auto-detects available CPU cores;
.B 1
forces sequential processing; any other value pins the thread-pool to
that count.
Has no effect when analyzing a single file.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print help message.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print version information.
.TP
.B \-\-supported\-languages
List compiled languages and extensions, then exit; no files required.
.TP
.B \-\-quiet
Suppress normal output; retain threshold-violation lines.
.TP
.B \-\-count\-anonymous\-closures
Emit anonymous functions as separate entries with synthesized labels. Default: off.
.TP
.B \-\-exclude\-path PATTERN
Exclude paths matching this regex; repeatable.
.TP
.B \-\-unreachable\-blocks\-threshold N
Exit 1 if any function exceeds this unreachable basic-block count (C/C++/Rust only).
.TP
.B \-\-report FILE
Write detailed per-function output in multi-file text mode. Ignored in single-file, matrix and structured modes.
.TP
.B \-\-baseline FILE
Gate only new over-threshold functions or regressions relative to this snapshot.
.TP
.B \-\-write\-baseline
Write current scores to --baseline and exit without gating; requires --baseline.
.TP
.B \-\-since REF
Gate functions overlapping lines changed between REF and the working tree. Output selection is unchanged.
.TP
.B \-\-changed
Equivalent to --since HEAD, including untracked files; mutually exclusive with --since.
.TP
.B \-\-explain METRIC
Explain a metric and how to lower it, then exit; no files required.
.TP
.B \-\-find\-duplicates
Report structural duplicates in recursive text mode. Shape equality does not prove safe extraction.
.TP
.B \-\-tier function|block
Select duplicate fingerprint granularity (default: function).
.TP
.B \-\-include\-fixture\-pairs
Retain intentional compliant/noncompliant fixture pairs in duplicate output.
.TP
.B \-\-include\-trivial\-duplicates
Retain small-body, low-repeat duplicate groups.
.TP
.B \-\-dump\-duplicates FILE
Write a JSON duplicate snapshot alongside --find-duplicates.
.TP
.B \-\-diff\-duplicates BEFORE AFTER
Compare two duplicate snapshots and exit; no corpus files required.
.SH FILTERS
Filter rules are specified in JSON files with the following optional fields:
.TP
.B file_patterns
Glob patterns for file paths.
Supports \fB*\fR, \fB**\fR, and \fB!\fR for negation.
.TP
.B function_patterns
Regular expression patterns for function names.
.TP
.B min_complexity
Minimum complexity threshold (inclusive).
.TP
.B max_complexity
Maximum complexity threshold (inclusive).
.PP
Example filter file:
.RS
.nf
{
    "file_patterns": ["src/**/*.c"],
    "function_patterns": ["^handle_"],
    "min_complexity": 10
}
.fi
.RE
.PP
Include and exclude file filters use the same matching predicate: at least
one positive pattern (if any), and no negative matches. Use positive patterns
to exclude directories; a negative-only exclude list removes their complement.
File exclusions happen at discovery; function criteria apply separately.
.PP
SARIF emits only functions with max(McCabe, cognitive) greater than 10,
independently of threshold flags. Use JSON or NDJSON for all score records.
.SH COMPLEXITY INDICATORS
.B knots
uses visual emoji indicators based on the maximum of McCabe and
Cognitive complexity:
.PP
.RS
.nf
1\-10   Good     \- Low complexity, easy to maintain
11\-20  Okay     \- Moderate complexity, may need attention
21\-49  Bad      \- High complexity, consider refactoring
50+    Critical \- Very high complexity, refactor immediately
.fi
.RE
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Successful analysis, no threshold violations.
.TP
.B 1
Error occurred (file not found, parse error, configuration error), or one or more
threshold violations were detected (when any \fB\-\-*\-threshold\fR flag is set).
.TP
.B 2
Command-line usage error.
.PP
Multi-file scans currently warn and skip unreadable or unparseable files.
Exit 0 does not guarantee every discovered input was analyzed.
.SH EXAMPLES
Analyze a single file:
.RS
.nf
knots path/to/file.c
.fi
.RE
.PP
Recursively analyze a directory:
.RS
.nf
knots \-r path/to/project/
.fi
.RE
.PP
CI gate \(em fail if any function has AIRD > 85:
.RS
.nf
knots \-r src/ \-\-aird\-threshold 85
.fi
.RE
.PP
Analyze a Rust project:
.RS
.nf
knots \-r src/
.fi
.RE
.PP
Parallel analysis of a large codebase:
.RS
.nf
knots \-r \-j 8 path/to/bigproject/
.fi
.RE
.PP
Analyze only C and C++ files in a mixed-language repository:
.RS
.nf
knots \-r \-l c \-l c++ path/to/project/
.fi
.RE
.PP
Analyze only Fortran files using an extension alias:
.RS
.nf
knots \-r \-l f90 path/to/project/
.fi
.RE
.PP
Corpus analysis \(em one JSON record per function, composable across files:
.RS
.nf
find . \-type f \e( \-name "*.c" \-o \-name "*.rs" \e) \-print0 | xargs \-0 \-r knots \-\-format ndjson > metrics.ndjson
.fi
.RE
.PP
Filter high-AIRD functions via jq:
.RS
.nf
find src/ \-type f \-name "*.rs" \-print0 | xargs \-0 \-r knots \-\-format ndjson | jq 'select(.aird > 70)'
.fi
.RE
.PP
Analyze files from a compilation database:
.RS
.nf
knots \-\-compile\-commands build/compile_commands.json
.fi
.RE
.PP
SARIF output for GitHub Code Scanning:
.RS
.nf
knots \-r \-\-format sarif src/ > knots.sarif
.fi
.RE
.SH FILES
.TP
.I report file
Written only with \fB\-\-report FILE\fR in multi-file text mode.
Contains per-function complexity details.
.TP
.I compile_commands.json
Compilation database used with \fB\-\-compile\-commands\fR.
